> A zero query gives a uniform retrieval

Two orthogonal memories and a zero query give equal logits. The next state is their mean(.5,.5), and the energy is minuslog2/beta. This attention operation has no trainable parameters.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/modern_hopfield_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");auto path=m::ModernHopfield(n::zeros({1,2}),n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{1,0,0,1},{2,2}),8);auto values=n::concat({path.attention.reshape({2}),path.next.reshape({2}),path.energy},0);if(std::abs(path.energy.item()+std::log(2.)/8)>1e-8)return 1;
std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");auto v=values.to_vector<double>();for(size_t i=0;i<v.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,v[i]);n::save_npz("build/modern_hopfield_worked.npz",{{"values",values}});dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(v.size())).to_vector<double>(),v,"native values",{37,99,235}).title("A zero query gives a uniform retrieval").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/modern_hopfield_worked.svg");}
```
