> Complete preserved experiment

All mathematical components run natively. Optional TensorFlow recordings are absent; their comparisons are skipped rather than asserted. The source random seeds, parameter names and fixed three-epoch budgets remain visible. Diagnostics without fitting use their original fixed inputs. This is a teaching experiment, not a benchmark parity claim.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
// CMD: just run-nn modern_hopfield
// Training-free continuous Hopfield retrieval using FIT-only MNIST memories and
// actual energy derivatives.
//
// Port of tflow's modern_hopfield (common/{nn,ml}/modern_hopfield.h ->
// examples/nn/common/modern_hopfield.hpp). Data: tflow's saliency MNIST pools
// (paths::Dataset("saliency"), `just autoencoder-assets` in tflow_examples; 1000 fit
// / 200 validation / 200 test), half-pixel bilinear 28 -> 8 gray. FIT-only 64-pixel
// mean; every vector centered and L2-normalized. The first fit image of each class
// gives the 10 stored unit-norm patterns. Queries: 100 noisy copies (10 per memory,
// + .15 N(0, 1) per coordinate from tflow's Gaussian bank 24001, no renormalization)
// and 200 heldout test images. Retrieval x' = softmax(beta x M^T) M is
// nn::scaled_dot_product_attention(x, M, M, scale = beta); 8 updates at beta 1, 8, 32.
// No trainable parameters, no training.
//
// Checks (as tflow): energy gradient == x - x' (actual autograd derivative) at every
// update; energy never increases (f32); zero query -> uniform attention; memory
// permutation preserves retrieval; fixed inputs repeat bit-exactly; single-row batch
// parity; memory/query bytes immutable; complete records. TF parity: data (gray
// pools, memories, noise, queries) checked bit-identical to tflow's
// output/models/modern_hopfield/data.npz; trajectories, probes (full Jacobians) and
// metrics.tsv compared with TF's record. Deviations: no independent_audit.json.
// Options: data=DIR out=DIR tf=DIR threads=4. Output: output/nn/models/modern_hopfield.
// Editable experiment support: modern_hopfield.hpp
// Port of tflow's common/nn/modern_hopfield.h and common/ml/modern_hopfield.h:
// continuous modern Hopfield energy E(x) = .5 ||x||^2 - logsumexp(beta x M^T) / beta
// and the tied key/value retrieval x' = softmax(beta x M^T) M (no learned
// projections, no training), with actual energy derivatives w.r.t. state and
// memory and the full 64x64 retrieval Jacobian.
//
// tflow -> datamunge: the retrieval is nn::scaled_dot_product_attention(x, M, M)
// with scale = beta (plain path, weights returned); AddSymbolicGradients -> nn::grad.

// Editable experiment support: binary_energy_data.hpp
// Shared support for the 3.5 energy-based model ports (restricted_boltzmann,
// deep_belief, deep_boltzmann, energy_langevin, modern_hopfield): a port of
// tflow's common/ml/binary_energy_data.h (synthetic single-bar corpus, explicit
// mt19937 uniform banks, 12-pixel binary tiles) plus the program helpers those
// examples repeat (option parsing, .npz records, TF record comparison).
//
// Every random draw of these examples is an explicit uniform/Gaussian bank from
// std::mt19937(seed), so the ports reproduce tflow's data, Gibbs uniforms and
// Langevin innovations bit for bit; only the weight initialisation differs
// (nn's generator), which init=auto removes by replaying TF's initial arrays.


// Editable experiment support: binary_pixels.hpp
// Shared harness of the binary 8x8 MNIST autoregressive density ports
// (pixel_cnn, gated_pixel_cnn, made_density, pixel_rnn): the program body that
// tflow repeats in each of those .cc files, plus the model-independent part of
// tflow's common/ml/{pixel_cnn,gated_pixel_cnn,made_density,pixel_rnn}.h
// (teacher-forced Bernoulli likelihood, causal logit/input Jacobian, prefix-only
// ancestral sampling with MT19937 uniforms).
//
// Data: the 1000/200/200 MNIST pools of tflow's saliency assets (ae::LoadSaliency),
// half-pixel bilinear 28 -> 8 in double then float32 threshold >= .5, as tflow.
//
// tflow -> datamunge: session graphs -> eager calls, AddSymbolicGradients ->
// nn::grad, Adam train_op -> nn::Optimizer (Adam .003), SaveV2 -> final.npz.
// TF parity: init=auto (default) replays TF's recorded initial_arrays.npz from
// tflow's output/models/<name>[/<variant>] so the whole run follows TF's; every
// record is then compared with TF's and the replayed first-step records must
// match. Independently of the trajectory, TF's FINAL weights (model_arrays.npz)
// are loaded into a fresh model which must reproduce TF's test outputs.


// Editable experiment support: autoencoder.hpp
// Shared support for the autoencoder ports: a port of the parts of tflow's
// common/ml/{autoencoder,convolutional_autoencoder,variational_autoencoder,
// saliency}.h and common/nn/{convolutional_autoencoder,variational_autoencoder,
// smoothgrad}.h that convolutional_autoencoder and variational_autoencoder use.
//
// Data: the balanced 1000 fit / 200 validation / 200 test MNIST pools of
// $DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR/saliency/saliency_data.npz (tflow's `just
// autoencoder-assets`). Checkpoints are .npz files of the parameter store
// instead of TF SaveV2 bundles. Parameter initialisation uses datamunge's
// generator, so trajectories match tflow only statistically; batch orders and
// Gaussian noise banks are bit-identical to tflow's.


// Editable experiment support: checks.hpp
// Small runtime checks used by the executable nn examples. They stay on in
// Release builds and make the example exit nonzero on failure, so `just
// run-all-nn` doubles as a regression test against the recorded TF numbers.

// Editable experiment support: runtime.hpp
// Bounded demonstrations by default; opt into convergence experiments explicitly.


namespace example_runtime {

inline bool Full() {
  const char* value = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_EXAMPLES_FULL");
  return value && std::string(value) == "1";
}

template <typename T> T Limit(T requested, T quick_limit) {
  return Full() ? requested : std::min(requested, quick_limit);
}

inline void Describe() {
  if (!Full())
    std::cout << "Quick demonstration: bounded training; convergence metrics require "
                 "DATAMUNGE_EXAMPLES_FULL=1.\n";
}

}  // namespace example_runtime

namespace check {

inline void Require(bool condition, const std::string& message) {
  if (!condition) throw std::runtime_error(message);
}

// A short demonstration checks execution, derivatives and persistence; reaching
// a published accuracy/return requires the separately requested full schedule.
inline void TrainingQuality(bool condition, const std::string& message) {
  if (example_runtime::Full()) Require(condition, message);
  else std::cout << "  full-training quality check deferred: " << message << '\n';
}

inline void Near(double actual, double expected, double tolerance, const std::string& message) {
  if (!std::isfinite(actual) || !std::isfinite(expected) || std::abs(actual - expected) > tolerance)
    throw std::runtime_error(message + ": got " + std::to_string(actual) + ", expected " + std::to_string(expected));
}

/// Expects `f` to throw; returns the message.
template <typename F>
std::string Throws(F&& f, const std::string& message) {
  try {
    f();
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    return e.what();
  }
  throw std::runtime_error(message + ": expected an exception");
}

}  // namespace check

inline void Header(const std::string& title) {
  const std::size_t pad = title.size() < 60 ? 60 - title.size() : 0;
  std::cout << "\n== " << title << " " << std::string(pad, '=') << "\n";
}

// Editable experiment support: paths.hpp
// Where the nn example ports read datasets and write their outputs.
//
// Datasets: $DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR, or the user's cache. Public datasets are
// prepared by the example data loaders when first needed.
// Outputs (checkpoints, histories, fixtures): $DATAMUNGE_OUTPUT_DIR, or
// output/nn relative to the working directory (`just run-nn` runs from the
// repository root). Both are created on demand by the caller.


// Editable experiment support: dataset_assets.hpp
namespace dataset_assets {
inline std::string DataRoot(){return dm::datasets::data_home();}
inline void EnsureSaliency(const std::string& directory){dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets",std::filesystem::path(directory).parent_path().string());}
inline dm::nn::ImageDataset LoadCifar10(const std::string& directory,const std::string& split){dm::datasets::fetch("cifar10",directory);return dm::nn::load_cifar10(directory,split);}
}

namespace paths {

inline std::filesystem::path DataRoot() {
return dm::datasets::data_home();
}

/// DataRoot() / name, e.g. Dataset("mnist").
inline std::filesystem::path Dataset(const std::string& name) { return DataRoot() / name; }

inline std::filesystem::path OutputRoot() {
return std::filesystem::absolute("build/generative-models");
}

/// OutputRoot() / relative, created as a directory.
inline std::filesystem::path OutputDir(const std::string& relative) {
  auto dir = OutputRoot() / relative;
  std::filesystem::create_directories(dir);
  return dir;
}

}  // namespace paths

namespace ae {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;

// ---- data ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

using SaliencyData=datamunge::nn::models::SaliencyData;

inline SaliencyData Rows(const SaliencyData& d, const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) {
  return {nn::take_rows(d.images, rows), nn::take_rows(d.labels, rows), nn::take_rows(d.source, rows)};
}

inline nn::Tensor Find(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays, const std::string& name) {
  for (const auto& [key, value] : arrays)
    if (key == name) return value;
  throw std::runtime_error("missing array " + name);
}

/// The fit, validation and test pools with tflow's integrity checks.
inline std::vector<SaliencyData> LoadSaliency(const std::filesystem::path&root){dataset_assets::EnsureSaliency(root.string());return nn::models::LoadSaliency(root);}

/// Copies tflow's provenance files next to the outputs when they exist.
inline void CopyManifests(const std::filesystem::path& data, const std::filesystem::path& root) {
  const auto opts = std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing;
  if (std::filesystem::exists(data / "manifest.json"))
    std::filesystem::copy_file(data / "manifest.json", root / "data_manifest.json", opts);
  const auto source = paths::Dataset("autoencoder") / "source_manifest.json";
  if (std::filesystem::exists(source)) std::filesystem::copy_file(source, root / "source_manifest.json", opts);
}

inline nn::Tensor GaussianNoise(const nn::Shape& shape,std::int64_t samples,std::uint32_t seed){return nn::models::GaussianNoise(shape,samples,seed); }
}

// Editable experiment support: tf_replay.hpp
// Small helpers the 4.2 sequence-task ports share for working with tflow's
// recorded runs: named-array maps (tflow's `std::map<std::string, tf::Tensor>`
// batches), row selection, exact/approximate comparisons, loading TF's
// initial_arrays.npz into a ParameterStore and reading history.tsv columns.
//
// A tflow run directory (tflow's output/models/<name>) holds initial_arrays.npz,
// first_batch.npz, initial_gradients.npz, history.tsv and model_arrays.npz.
// Replaying the run from TF's own initial weights with the same batch order
// (nn::BatchOrder reproduces tflow's) and the same optimizer checks the port
// numerically, independently of the random initialisation.





namespace replay {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;
using nn::Tensor;
using Map = std::map<std::string, Tensor>;

/// tflow's recorded output directory for an example (its output/models/<name>).
inline std::filesystem::path TfModels(const std::string& name) {
  return paths::DataRoot().parent_path() / "models" / name;
}

inline Tensor Get(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays, const std::string& key) {
  for (const auto& [name, t] : arrays)
    if (name == key) return t;
  throw std::runtime_error("missing array " + key);
}

inline Map ToMap(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays) { return {arrays.begin(), arrays.end()}; }
inline nn::NamedTensors ToNamed(const Map& m) { return {m.begin(), m.end()}; }

/// Rows `rows` (axis 0) of every array.
inline Map Rows(const Map& m, const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) {
  Map out;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : m) out[k] = nn::take_rows(v, rows);
  return out;
}

/// {key: arrays["<split>_<key>"]} for each key.
inline Map Split(const nn::NamedTensors& arrays, const std::string& split, const std::vector<std::string>& keys) {
  Map out;
  for (const auto& k : keys) out[k] = Get(arrays, split + "_" + k);
  return out;
}

inline double MaxAbsDiff(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  const auto x = a.to_vector<double>(), y = b.to_vector<double>();
  check::Require(x.size() == y.size(), "compared tensors have the same size");
  double m = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i) m = std::max(m, std::abs(x[i] - y[i]));
  return m;
}

/// Bit-identical values (dtype and shape included).
inline bool SameBits(const Tensor& a, const Tensor& b) {
  if (a.dtype() != b.dtype() || a.shape() != b.shape()) return false;
  auto same = [](const auto& x, const auto& y) {
    return x.size() == y.size() && (x.empty() || std::memcmp(x.data(), y.data(), x.size() * sizeof(x[0])) == 0);
  };
  switch (a.dtype()) {
    case nn::DType::Float32: return same(a.to_vector<float>(), b.to_vector<float>());
    case nn::DType::Float64: return same(a.to_vector<double>(), b.to_vector<double>());
    case nn::DType::Int32: return same(a.to_vector<std::int32_t>(), b.to_vector<std::int32_t>());
    default: return same(a.to_vector<std::int64_t>(), b.to_vector<std::int64_t>());
  }
}

inline bool SameBits(const Map& a, const Map& b) {
  if (a.size() != b.size()) return false;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (!b.count(k) || !SameBits(v, b.at(k))) return false;
  return true;
}

/// Copies of every parameter, by name.
inline Map Arrays(const nn::ParameterStore& p) {
  Map out;
  for (const auto& name : p.names()) out[name] = p.at(name).detach().clone();
  return out;
}

/// Gradients aligned with p.names(), by name.
inline Map Named(const nn::ParameterStore& p, const std::vector<Tensor>& g) {
  Map out;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < g.size(); ++i) out[p.names()[i]] = g[i].defined() ? g[i].detach() : nn::zeros_like(p.parameters()[i]).detach();
  return out;
}

/// Overwrites every parameter of `p` from an .npz (e.g. TF's initial_arrays.npz),
/// which must hold exactly p's names.
inline void LoadInto(nn::ParameterStore& p, const std::filesystem::path& file) {
  const auto arrays = nn::load_npz(file.string());
  check::Require(arrays.size() == p.size(), "array file covers exactly the model's parameters: " + file.string());
  for (const auto& [name, value] : arrays) {
    check::Require(p.contains(name), "array " + name + " is a model parameter");
    p.set(name, nn::cast(value, p.at(name).dtype()));
  }
}

/// max |a[k] - b[k]| over the keys of `a` (all must exist in `b`).
inline double MaxDiff(const Map& a, const Map& b) {
  double m = 0;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a) {
    check::Require(b.count(k) > 0, "reference has array " + k);
    m = std::max(m, MaxAbsDiff(v, b.at(k)));
  }
  return m;
}
inline double MaxDiff(const Map& a, const std::filesystem::path& file) { return MaxDiff(a, ToMap(nn::load_npz(file.string()))); }

/// Column `column` (0-based) of a tab-separated history file with a header line.
inline std::vector<double> History(const std::filesystem::path& file, int column = 1) {
  std::ifstream       in(file);
  std::string         line;
  std::vector<double> out;
  std::getline(in, line);
  while (std::getline(in, line)) {
    std::stringstream ss(line);
    std::string       cell;
    for (int c = 0; c <= column && std::getline(ss, cell, '\t'); ++c)
      if (c == column) out.push_back(std::stod(cell));
  }
  return out;
}

inline nn::OptimizerConfig Adam() {
  nn::OptimizerConfig c;
  c.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  return c;
}

/// Copies `files` from `from` to `to` when present.
inline void CopyAssets(const std::filesystem::path& from, const std::filesystem::path& to,
                       const std::vector<std::string>& files) {
  for (const auto& f : files)
    if (std::filesystem::exists(from / f))
      std::filesystem::copy_file(from / f, to / f, std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}

}  // namespace replay

namespace bpix {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;
namespace fs = std::filesystem;
using nn::Tensor;
using Map = replay::Map;

// ---- small helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

inline Tensor Floats(const std::vector<float>& v, const nn::Shape& s) {
  return nn::from_vector(v, s);
}

/// tflow's Png: every 8x8 image as a 64x64 tile (8x nearest), `columns` per row,
/// gray 220 background, floor(v * 255 + .5); `rgb` images use (v + 1) * 127.5
/// with clamping when `signed_range`, else 255 clamp(v, 0, 1).
inline void Png(const fs::path& path, const Tensor& images, int columns, int mode = 0) {
  const auto         n = images.size(0), c = images.size(3);
  const auto         v    = images.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  const std::int64_t rows = (n + columns - 1) / columns, H = rows * 64, W = columns * 64;
  std::vector<float> out(static_cast<std::size_t>(H * W * 3), 220.f);
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b)
    for (int y = 0; y < 64; ++y)
      for (int x = 0; x < 64; ++x)
        for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
          const double value =
              v[static_cast<std::size_t>(((b * 8 + y / 8) * 8 + x / 8) * c + (c == 1 ? 0 : k))];
          double byte = mode == 0   ? std::floor(value * 255 + .5)
                        : mode == 1 ? std::floor(std::clamp((value + 1) * 127.5, 0., 255.) + .5)
                                    : std::floor(255 * std::clamp(value, 0., 1.) + .5);
          out[static_cast<std::size_t>(
              ((b / columns * 64 + y) * W + b % columns * 64 + x) * 3 + k)] = float(byte);
        }
  nn::save_png(Floats(out, {H, W, 3}), path.string(), 0, 255);
}

/// Writes a [H, W, 3] uint8-valued byte image.
inline void
PngBytes(const fs::path& path, const std::vector<float>& bytes, std::int64_t h, std::int64_t w) {
  nn::save_png(Floats(bytes, {h, w, 3}), path.string(), 0, 255);
}

inline void RequireFinite(const Map& m, const std::string& what) {
  for (const auto& [k, v] : m)
    if (v.dtype() == nn::DType::Float32)
      for (float x : v.contiguous().to_vector<float>())
        check::Require(std::isfinite(x), what);
}

inline std::string Bits(const Tensor& t) {
  const auto c = t.contiguous();
  switch (c.dtype()) {
    case nn::DType::Float32: {
      const auto v = c.to_vector<float>();
      return {reinterpret_cast<const char*>(v.data()), v.size() * sizeof(float)};
    }
    case nn::DType::Float64: {
      const auto v = c.to_vector<double>();
      return {reinterpret_cast<const char*>(v.data()), v.size() * sizeof(double)};
    }
    default: {
      const auto v = c.to_vector<std::int32_t>();
      return {reinterpret_cast<const char*>(v.data()), v.size() * sizeof(std::int32_t)};
    }
  }
}

inline bool SameBits(const Map& a, const Map& b) {
  if (a.size() != b.size())
    return false;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : a)
    if (!b.count(k) || Bits(v) != Bits(b.at(k)) || v.shape() != b.at(k).shape())
      return false;
  return true;
}

// ---- options ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

struct Options {
  int         epochs = 3, threads = 4;
  fs::path    data    = paths::Dataset("saliency"), out, tf;
  std::string init    = "auto";
  bool        verbose = false;
};

/// epochs=N data=DIR out=DIR init=auto|tf|nn|PATH tf=DIR threads=N verbose=0|1
inline Options ParseOptions(int argc, char** argv, const std::string& name, const fs::path& data) {
  Options o;
  o.data = data;
  o.tf   = replay::TfModels(name);
  for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
    const std::string a = argv[i];
    const auto        e = a.find('=');
    check::Require(
        e != std::string::npos,
        "expected key=value (epochs= data= out= init= tf= threads= verbose=)");
    const std::string k = a.substr(0, e), v = a.substr(e + 1);
    if (k == "epochs")
      o.epochs = std::stoi(v);
    else if (k == "data")
      o.data = v;
    else if (k == "out")
      o.out = v;
    else if (k == "init")
      o.init = v;
    else if (k == "tf")
      o.tf = v;
    else if (k == "threads")
      o.threads = std::stoi(v);
    else if (k == "verbose")
      o.verbose = v != "0";
    else
      throw std::invalid_argument(
          "epochs=N data=PATH out=PATH init=auto|tf|nn|PATH tf=DIR threads=N verbose=0|1");
  }
  check::Require(
      o.epochs > 0 && o.epochs <= 100, "three cheap default epochs or explicit 1..100 override");
  if (o.out.empty())
    o.out = paths::OutputRoot() / "models" / name;
  fs::create_directories(o.out);
  if (o.threads > 0)
    nn::set_num_threads(o.threads);
  return o;
}

/// The initial arrays to replay (empty: nn's generator). `tf` is the TF run directory.
inline fs::path InitFile(const std::string& init, const fs::path& tf) {
  if (init == "nn")
    return {};
  if (init == "auto" || init == "tf") {
    const auto f = tf / "initial_arrays.npz";
    if (init == "tf")
      check::Require(fs::exists(f), "init=tf needs " + f.string());
    return fs::exists(f) ? f : fs::path();
  }
  check::Require(fs::exists(init), "init file " + init + " missing");
  return init;
}

/// Max |ours - TF| over the arrays both records share (-1 when TF's file is missing);
/// `relative`: max |ours - TF| / (1 + |TF|).
inline double Compare(
    const fs::path&    tf,
    const std::string& file,
    const Map&         ours,
    bool               verbose  = false,
    bool               relative = false) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / file)) {
    std::printf("  vs TF %-28s (no TF record)\n", file.c_str());
    return -1;
  }
  const auto theirs = replay::ToMap(nn::load_npz((tf / file).string()));
  double     m      = 0;
  int        shared = 0;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : ours) {
    if (!theirs.count(k) || theirs.at(k).numel() != v.numel())
      continue;
    const auto x = nn::cast(v, nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>(),
               y = nn::cast(theirs.at(k), nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
    double d     = 0;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < x.size(); ++i)
      d = std::max(d, std::abs(x[i] - y[i]) / (relative ? 1 + std::abs(y[i]) : 1.));
    if (verbose)
      std::printf("      %-24s %.3g\n", k.c_str(), d);
    m = std::max(m, d);
    ++shared;
  }
  std::printf(
      "  vs TF %-28s max |ours - TF|%s = %.3g (%d arrays)\n",
      file.c_str(),
      relative ? "/(1+|TF|)" : "",
      m,
      shared);
  return m;
}

/// Fraction of equal elements of `key` in ours vs TF's record.
inline double
Agreement(const fs::path& tf, const std::string& file, const Map& ours, const std::string& key) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / file))
    return -1;
  const auto theirs = replay::ToMap(nn::load_npz((tf / file).string()));
  if (!theirs.count(key))
    return -1;
  const auto a = nn::cast(ours.at(key), nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
  const auto b = nn::cast(theirs.at(key), nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
  if (a.size() != b.size())
    return -1;
  std::size_t same = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i)
    same += a[i] == b[i];
  return double(same) / double(a.size());
}

// ---- data -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/// tflow's half-pixel bilinear 28 -> 8 resize (double accumulation, float result).
inline Tensor Resize8(const Tensor& images) {
return nn::models::BigGanResize8(images);
}

}

namespace ebm {

namespace nn = datamunge::nn;
namespace fs = std::filesystem;
using nn::Tensor;
using Map = replay::Map;

// ---- random banks and data -------------------------------------------------------------

/// tflow's ml::BinaryUniform: (mt19937() + .5) / 2^32 as [n, dimensions] float32 (float64 when wide).
inline Tensor BinaryUniform(std::int64_t n, std::int64_t dimensions, std::uint32_t seed, bool wide = false) {
return nn::MidpointUniform(n,dimensions,seed,wide?nn::DType::Float64:nn::DType::Float32);
}

/// tflow's nn::GaussianNoise bank [n, dimensions] (float32, or float64 when wide).
inline Tensor Gaussian(std::int64_t n, std::uint32_t seed, bool wide = false, std::int64_t dimensions = 2) {
  const Tensor raw = nn::reshape(ae::GaussianNoise({n, dimensions}, 1, seed), {n, dimensions});
  return wide ? raw : nn::cast(raw, nn::DType::Float32);
}

inline Tensor Ints(const std::vector<std::int32_t>& v) { return nn::from_vector(v, {std::int64_t(v.size())}); }

/// tflow's ml::BinaryBars: uniformly one of 4 vertical / 2 horizontal bars of a 2x4
/// grid, each bit flipped with probability .05. Keys points/uniform/components/source_ids.
inline Map BinaryBars(std::int64_t n, std::uint32_t seed, int offset) {
auto x=nn::models::BinaryBars(n,seed,offset);return {{"points",x.points},{"uniform",x.uniforms},{"components",x.components},{"source_ids",x.source_ids}};
}

/// tflow's nn::RbmBinaryStates: all 2^bits binary rows, bit j of row b = (b >> j) & 1.
inline Tensor BinaryStates(int bits) {
return nn::models::BinaryStates(bits);
}

/// tflow's ml::BinaryTiles: every row of `values` [n, bits] as a (bits / width) x width
/// grid of 12-pixel cells, `columns` tiles per row, 4-pixel gray-220 gutters.
inline void BinaryTiles(const fs::path& path, const Tensor& values, int columns, int width = 4) {
  const auto n = values.size(0), bits = values.size(1);
  check::Require(bits % width == 0, "binary tiles rectangular");
  const std::int64_t height = bits / width, px = width * 12 + 4, py = height * 12 + 4;
  const std::int64_t H = ((n + columns - 1) / columns) * py, W = columns * px;
  const auto         v = values.contiguous().to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<float> rgb(static_cast<std::size_t>(H * W * 3), 220.f);
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b)
    for (std::int64_t y = 0; y < height * 12; ++y)
      for (std::int64_t x = 0; x < width * 12; ++x) {
        const double p = v[static_cast<std::size_t>(b * bits + (y / 12) * width + x / 12)];
        check::Require(std::isfinite(p) && p >= 0 && p <= 1, "binary tiles probabilities");
        for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c)
          rgb[static_cast<std::size_t>(((b / columns * py + y) * W + b % columns * px + x) * 3 + c)] = float(std::floor(p * 255 + .5));
      }
  bpix::PngBytes(path, rgb, H, W);
}

// ---- records -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

inline Tensor Rows(const Tensor& x, const std::vector<std::int64_t>& rows) { return nn::take_rows(x, rows); }
inline std::vector<std::int64_t> Range(std::int64_t n) {
  std::vector<std::int64_t> r(static_cast<std::size_t>(n));
  for (std::int64_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) r[i] = i;
  return r;
}
inline void        Save(const fs::path& file, const Map& m) { nn::save_npz(file.string(), replay::ToNamed(m)); }
inline Map         Load(const fs::path& file) { return replay::ToMap(nn::load_npz(file.string())); }
inline std::string Bits(const Tensor& t) { return bpix::Bits(t); }
inline double      Scalar(const Map& m, const std::string& k) { return nn::cast(m.at(k), nn::DType::Float64).item<double>(); }

inline Map Detached(const Map& m) {
  Map out;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : m) out[k] = v.detach();
  return out;
}
inline std::vector<std::string> Snapshot(const Map& arrays) {
  std::vector<std::string> out;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : arrays) out.push_back(Bits(v));
  return out;
}
/// Bit-identical copies of every array of `ours` in TF's record `file` (missing file: true).
inline bool SameAsTf(const fs::path& tf, const std::string& file, const Map& ours) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / file)) return true;
  const auto theirs = Load(tf / file);
  for (const auto& [k, v] : ours)
    if (!theirs.count(k) || Bits(theirs.at(k)) != Bits(v) || theirs.at(k).shape() != v.shape()) return false;
  return true;
}
/// Fraction of equal elements over the shared keys of `file` (all, or only `keys`;
/// -1 without a TF record). Used for sampled binary states.
inline double Agreement(const fs::path& tf, const std::string& file, const Map& ours, const std::vector<std::string>& keys = {}) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / file)) return -1;
  const auto  theirs = Load(tf / file);
  std::size_t same = 0, total = 0;
  for (const auto& [k, v] : ours) {
    if (!keys.empty() && std::find(keys.begin(), keys.end(), k) == keys.end()) continue;
    if (!theirs.count(k) || theirs.at(k).numel() != v.numel()) continue;
    const auto a = nn::cast(v, nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>(), b = nn::cast(theirs.at(k), nn::DType::Float64).to_vector<double>();
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); ++i) same += a[i] == b[i];
    total += a.size();
  }
  return total ? double(same) / double(total) : -1;
}

inline nn::OptimizerConfig Sgd() { return {}; }
inline nn::OptimizerConfig Adam() {
  nn::OptimizerConfig c;
  c.kind = nn::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  return c;
}

/// Gradients of `loss` w.r.t. every parameter of `p`, by name.
inline Map ParameterGradients(const nn::ParameterStore& p, const Tensor& loss) {
  return replay::Named(p, nn::grad(loss, p.parameters()));
}

/// Overwrites the parameters of `p` from `arrays` (names `prefix + name`).
inline void SetFrom(nn::ParameterStore& p, const Map& arrays, const std::string& prefix = "") {
  for (const auto& name : p.names()) {
    check::Require(arrays.count(prefix + name) > 0, "array " + prefix + name + " present");
    p.set(name, nn::cast(arrays.at(prefix + name), p.at(name).dtype()));
  }
}

/// Finds a frozen checkpoint in `dir`: final.npz (our ports) or model_arrays.npz (TF's restored weights).
inline fs::path FrozenFile(const fs::path& dir) {
  if (fs::exists(dir / "final.npz")) return dir / "final.npz";
  if (fs::exists(dir / "model_arrays.npz")) return dir / "model_arrays.npz";
  return {};
}
/// "ours" (our port's output), "tf" (tflow's recorded run), "auto" (ours when present, else TF) or a directory.
inline fs::path FrozenDir(const std::string& choice, const fs::path& ours, const fs::path& tf) {
  if (choice == "ours") return ours;
  if (choice == "tf") return tf;
  if (choice == "auto") return FrozenFile(ours).empty() ? tf : ours;
  return choice;
}

// ---- options -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

struct Options {
  int                                epochs = 3, threads = 4;
  fs::path                           out, tf;
  std::string                        init = "auto";
  std::map<std::string, std::string> extra;  // source= / data=
};

/// key=value options: epochs out init tf threads + `extra` (name -> default).
inline Options ParseOptions(int argc, char** argv, const std::string& name, const std::map<std::string, std::string>& extra,
                            const std::string& usage) {
  Options o;
  o.tf    = replay::TfModels(name);
  o.extra = extra;
  for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i) {
    const std::string a = argv[i];
    const auto        e = a.find('=');
    if (e == std::string::npos) throw std::invalid_argument(usage);
    const std::string k = a.substr(0, e), v = a.substr(e + 1);
    if (k == "epochs") o.epochs = std::stoi(v);
    else if (k == "out") o.out = v;
    else if (k == "init") o.init = v;
    else if (k == "tf") o.tf = v;
    else if (k == "threads") o.threads = std::stoi(v);
    else if (o.extra.count(k)) o.extra[k] = v;
    else throw std::invalid_argument(usage);
  }
  check::Require(o.epochs > 0 && o.epochs <= 100, "three cheap default epochs or explicit 1..100 override");
  if (o.out.empty()) o.out = paths::OutputRoot() / "models" / name;
  fs::create_directories(o.out);
  if (o.threads > 0) nn::set_num_threads(o.threads);
  return o;
}

/// Bit-identity of our data record with TF's data.npz on `keys`.
inline void CheckData(const fs::path& tf, const Map& data, const std::vector<std::string>& keys) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / "data.npz")) return;
  const auto theirs = Load(tf / "data.npz");
  for (const auto& k : keys)
    check::Require(theirs.count(k) && Bits(theirs.at(k)) == Bits(data.at(k)), "data bit-identical to TF's data.npz: " + k);
  std::cout << "data: " << keys.size() << " arrays bit-identical to TF's data.npz\n";
}

/// Prints ours vs TF per epoch for history column `column`.
inline void CompareHistory(const fs::path& ours, const fs::path& tf, int column, const std::string& what) {
  if (!fs::exists(tf / "history.tsv")) return;
  const auto a = replay::History(ours / "history.tsv", column), b = replay::History(tf / "history.tsv", column);
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < std::min(a.size(), b.size()); ++i)
    std::printf("  epoch %zu %s ours %.7f TF %.7f\n", i + 1, what.c_str(), a[i], b[i]);
}

}  // namespace ebm

// Editable experiment support: restricted_boltzmann.hpp
// Port of tflow's common/nn/restricted_boltzmann.h and common/ml/restricted_boltzmann.h:
// Bernoulli RBM energy, conditionals, exact (enumerated) log partition and a
// sampled CD1 stopped-chain surrogate trained with SGD(.05).
//
// tflow -> datamunge: graph/session model -> class over a nn::ParameterStore
// (names W / visible_bias / hidden_bias as tflow, so TF's .npz arrays load
// directly); AddSymbolicGradients -> nn::grad; SaveV2 -> final.npz.

namespace ebm {
using nn::models::RbmParameters;
using nn::models::RbmHidden;
using nn::models::RbmVisible;
using nn::models::RbmFreeEnergy;
using nn::models::LogSumExp;
using nn::models::RbmLogPartition;
using nn::models::RbmGibbsPath;
using nn::models::RbmGibbs;
/// tflow's ml::RestrictedBoltzmannModel (seed 21003; 8x4 -> 44 parameters / 3 tensors).
class RestrictedBoltzmannModel {
 public:
  nn::ParameterStore             store;
  int                            visible, hidden;


  explicit RestrictedBoltzmannModel(bool training = true, int visible_count = 8, int hidden_count = 4, std::uint64_t seed = 21003)
      : store(seed), visible(visible_count), hidden(hidden_count) {
    RbmParameters(store, visible, hidden);

  }
  Tensor Nll(const Tensor& v) {
    const Tensor logp = nn::neg(nn::add(RbmFreeEnergy(store, v), RbmLogPartition(store, visible)));
    return nn::neg(nn::mean(logp, {0}));
  }
  /// mean(F(v0) - F(stop(v1))): derivative = -(positive - negative CD statistics).
  Tensor CdLoss(const Tensor& v, const Tensor& u, const Tensor& w) {
    const auto path = RbmGibbs(store, v, u, w);
    return nn::mean(nn::sub(RbmFreeEnergy(store, v), RbmFreeEnergy(store, nn::stop_gradient(path.visible))), {0});
  }
  Map Evaluate(const Tensor& v) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    const Tensor    fe = RbmFreeEnergy(store, v), logz = RbmLogPartition(store, visible);
    const Tensor    logp = nn::neg(nn::add(fe, logz));
    return {{"free_energy", fe}, {"log_partition", logz}, {"log_probability", logp},
            {"nll", nn::neg(nn::mean(logp, {0}))}, {"hidden_probability", RbmHidden(store, v)}};
  }
  Map Gibbs(const Tensor& v, const Tensor& u, const Tensor& w, bool include_loss = true) {
    nn::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto      p = RbmGibbs(store, v, u, w);
    Map             out{{"hidden_probability", p.hidden_probability}, {"hidden", p.hidden},
                        {"visible_probability", p.visible_probability}, {"visible", p.visible},
                        {"negative_hidden_probability", p.negative_hidden_probability}};
    if (include_loss) out["cd_surrogate"] = CdLoss(v, u, w);
    return out;
  }
  Map  Gradient(const Tensor& v, const Tensor& u, const Tensor& w, bool exact = false) {
    return ParameterGradients(store, exact ? Nll(v) : CdLoss(v, u, w));
  }

  Map  Arrays() const { return replay::Arrays(store); }
  std::vector<std::string> Snapshot() const { return ebm::Snapshot(Arrays()); }
};

}  // namespace ebm

namespace ebm {
using nn::models::ModernHopfieldPath;
using nn::models::ModernHopfield;
/// tflow's ml::ModernHopfieldModel: stateless; Evaluate(x [n, 64], memory [10, 64], beta).
class ModernHopfieldModel {
 public:
  Map Evaluate(const Tensor& x, const Tensor& stored, float beta, bool full_jacobian = false) const {
    check::Require(beta > 0, "positive Hopfield inverse temperature");
    const Tensor state = x.detach().clone().requires_grad_(true), memory = stored.detach().clone().requires_grad_(true);
    const auto   path = ModernHopfield(state, memory, beta);
    nn::GradOptions keep;
    keep.retain_graph = true;
    const auto g      = nn::grad({nn::sum(path.energy)}, {state, memory}, {}, keep);
    Map        out{{"logits", path.logits.detach()},  {"attention", path.attention.detach()}, {"next", path.next.detach()},
                   {"energy", path.energy.detach()},  {"state_gradient", g[0].detach()},      {"memory_gradient", g[1].detach()}};
    if (full_jacobian) {
      const auto n = x.size(0);
      for (int row = 0; row < 64; ++row) {
        std::vector<float> e(static_cast<std::size_t>(n * 64), 0.f);
        for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b) e[b * 64 + row] = 1.f;
        out["jacobian_row" + std::to_string(row)] = nn::grad({path.next}, {state}, {nn::from_vector(e, {n, 64})}, keep)[0].detach();
      }
    }
    return out;
  }
};

}  // namespace ebm

namespace {

using namespace ebm;

std::pair<Tensor, Tensor> Encode(const Tensor& x, const std::vector<double>& center) {
  const auto          v = x.to_vector<float>();
  const auto          n = x.size(0);
  std::vector<float>  values(v.size());
  std::vector<double> norms(n);
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b) {
    double norm = 0;
    for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) norm += std::pow(double(v[b * 64 + j]) - center[j], 2);
    norm = std::sqrt(norm);
    check::Require(norm > 1e-6, "nonzero centered image norm");
    norms[b] = norm;
    for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) values[b * 64 + j] = float((double(v[b * 64 + j]) - center[j]) / norm);
  }
  return {nn::from_vector(values, {n, 64}), nn::from_vector(norms, {n})};
}

void Png(const fs::path& path, const Tensor& images, int columns) { bpix::Png(path, nn::reshape(images, {-1, 8, 8, 1}), columns, 2); }

void Heatmap(const fs::path& path, const Tensor& weights) {
  const auto         n = weights.size(0);
  const auto         w = weights.to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<float> rgb(static_cast<std::size_t>(n * 20 * 300 * 3), 220.f);
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b)
    for (int m = 0; m < 10; ++m) {
      const double a = w[b * 10 + m], color[] = {255 * (1 - a), 255 * (1 - .65 * a), 255};
      for (int y = 0; y < 19; ++y)
        for (int x = 0; x < 29; ++x)
          for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) rgb[static_cast<std::size_t>(((b * 20 + y) * 300 + m * 30 + x) * 3 + c)] = float(std::floor(color[c] + .5));
    }
  bpix::PngBytes(path, rgb, n * 20, 300);
}

Tensor WeightedImages(const Tensor& weights, const Tensor& gray) {
  const auto         n = weights.size(0);
  const auto         w = weights.to_vector<float>(), g = gray.to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<float> out(static_cast<std::size_t>(n * 64));
  for (std::int64_t b = 0; b < n; ++b)
    for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) {
      double sum = 0;
      for (int m = 0; m < 10; ++m) sum += double(w[b * 10 + m]) * g[m * 64 + j];
      out[b * 64 + j] = float(sum);
    }
  return nn::from_vector(out, {n, 64});
}

int Argmax(const std::vector<float>& a, std::int64_t b) {
  int best = 0;
  for (int c = 1; c < 10; ++c)
    if (a[b * 10 + c] > a[b * 10 + best]) best = c;
  return best;
}

void Run(const Options& o) {
  const fs::path root = o.out, tf = o.tf, data_root = o.extra.at("data");
  const auto     pools = ae::LoadSaliency(data_root);
  Map            data;
  std::vector<Tensor> gray;
  for (int k = 0; k < 3; ++k) {
    const std::string split = k == 0 ? "fit" : k == 1 ? "validation" : "test";
    gray.push_back(nn::reshape(bpix::Resize8(pools[k].images), {-1, 64}));
    data[split + "_original"]   = pools[k].images;
    data[split + "_gray"]       = gray.back();
    data[split + "_labels"]     = pools[k].labels;
    data[split + "_source_ids"] = pools[k].source;
  }
  ae::CopyManifests(data_root, root);
  const auto          fit = gray[0].to_vector<float>();
  std::vector<double> center(64);
  for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) {
    double mean = 0;
    for (int b = 0; b < 1000; ++b) mean += double(fit[b * 64 + j]) / 1000;
    center[j] = mean;
  }
  const auto                fit_labels = pools[0].labels.to_vector<std::int32_t>(), fit_source = pools[0].source.to_vector<std::int32_t>();
  const auto                test_labels = pools[2].labels.to_vector<std::int32_t>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> selected;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c)
    for (int b = 0; b < 1000; ++b)
      if (fit_labels[b] == c) {
        selected.push_back(b);
        break;
      }
  check::Require(selected.size() == 10, "one fit memory per class");
  const Tensor memory_gray        = Rows(gray[0], selected);
  const auto [memory, norms]      = Encode(memory_gray, center);
  const auto [heldout, heldout_n] = Encode(gray[2], center);
  const auto raw_noise = ae::GaussianNoise({100, 64}, 1, 24001).to_vector<double>();
  const auto mv = memory.to_vector<float>(), hv = heldout.to_vector<float>();
  const auto nv = norms.to_vector<double>();
  std::vector<float>        queries(300 * 64), noisy_gray(100 * 64);
  std::vector<std::int32_t> targets(300), memory_indices(10), memory_sources(10);
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) memory_indices[c] = int(selected[c]), memory_sources[c] = fit_source[selected[c]];
  for (int b = 0; b < 100; ++b) {
    targets[b] = b / 10;
    for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) {
      queries[b * 64 + j]    = float(double(mv[(b / 10) * 64 + j]) + .15 * raw_noise[b * 64 + j]);
      noisy_gray[b * 64 + j] = float(center[j] + nv[b / 10] * queries[b * 64 + j]);
    }
  }
  for (int b = 0; b < 200; ++b) {
    targets[100 + b] = test_labels[b];
    std::copy_n(hv.data() + b * 64, 64, queries.data() + (100 + b) * 64);
  }
  const Tensor queries_t = nn::from_vector(queries, {300, 64}), noisy_gray_t = nn::from_vector(noisy_gray, {100, 64});
  data["fit_center"]          = nn::from_vector(center, {64});
  data["memory_gray"]         = memory_gray;
  data["memory"]              = memory;
  data["memory_norms"]        = norms;
  data["memory_fit_indices"]  = Ints(memory_indices);
  data["memory_source_ids"]   = Ints(memory_sources);
  data["heldout"]             = heldout;
  data["heldout_norms"]       = heldout_n;
  data["noise"]               = nn::from_vector(raw_noise, {100, 64});
  data["queries"]             = queries_t;
  data["noisy_gray"]          = noisy_gray_t;
  data["target_memory_class"] = Ints(targets);
  std::vector<std::int64_t> gallery_indices, probe_indices;
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) gallery_indices.push_back(c * 10), probe_indices.push_back(c * 10);
  for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c)
    for (int b = 0; b < 200; ++b)
      if (test_labels[b] == c) {
        gallery_indices.push_back(100 + b);
        if (c < 6) probe_indices.push_back(100 + b);
        break;
      }
  std::vector<std::int32_t> gi(gallery_indices.begin(), gallery_indices.end()), pi(probe_indices.begin(), probe_indices.end());
  data["gallery_indices"] = Ints(gi);
  data["probe_indices"]   = Ints(pi);
  Save(root / "data.npz", data);
  CheckData(tf, data,
            {"fit_gray", "test_gray", "fit_center", "memory_gray", "memory", "memory_norms", "memory_fit_indices", "noise", "queries",
             "noisy_gray", "heldout", "target_memory_class", "gallery_indices", "probe_indices"});
  Png(root / "memories.png", memory_gray, 10);
  const ModernHopfieldModel model;
  const std::string         memory_bytes = Bits(memory), query_bytes = Bits(queries_t);
  std::ofstream             metrics(root / "metrics.tsv");
  metrics.precision(17);
  metrics << "beta\tnoisy_memory_initial_accuracy\tnoisy_memory_final_accuracy\theldout_initial_nearest_class_accuracy\theldout_final_"
             "class_accuracy\tmax_energy_increase\tfinal_update_max_residual\n";
  for (float beta : {1.f, 8.f, 32.f}) {
    const std::string   name = "beta" + std::to_string(int(beta));
    Tensor              state = queries_t;
    std::vector<Tensor> states{state}, energies, attentions, gradients, memory_gradients;
    Map                 first, last;
    double              energy_increase = 0, residual = 0;
    std::vector<float>  previous;
    for (int k = 0; k <= 8; ++k) {
      const auto out = model.Evaluate(state, memory, beta);
      if (!k) first = out;
      last              = out;
      const auto energy = out.at("energy").to_vector<float>();
      if (k)
        for (int b = 0; b < 300; ++b) energy_increase = std::max(energy_increase, double(energy[b]) - previous[b]);
      previous = energy;
      energies.push_back(out.at("energy"));
      attentions.push_back(out.at("attention"));
      gradients.push_back(out.at("state_gradient"));
      memory_gradients.push_back(out.at("memory_gradient"));
      const auto sg = out.at("state_gradient").to_vector<float>(), sv = state.to_vector<float>(), xv = out.at("next").to_vector<float>();
      for (std::size_t i = 0; i < sg.size(); ++i) {
        check::Near(sg[i], double(sv[i]) - xv[i], 2e-6, "energy gradient equals state minus attention retrieval");
        if (k == 8) residual = std::max(residual, std::abs(double(sv[i]) - xv[i]));
      }
      if (k < 8) {
        state = out.at("next");
        states.push_back(state);
      }
    }
    check::Require(energy_increase < 1e-5, "Hopfield retrieval energy does not increase within f32");
    Save(root / (name + "_trajectory.npz"), {{"states", nn::stack(states, 0)},
                                              {"energies", nn::stack(energies, 0)},
                                              {"attentions", nn::stack(attentions, 0)},
                                              {"state_gradients", nn::stack(gradients, 0)},
                                              {"memory_gradients", nn::stack(memory_gradients, 0)}});
    const Tensor probes = Rows(queries_t, probe_indices);
    Save(root / (name + "_probe.npz"), model.Evaluate(probes, memory, beta, true));
    const auto uniform = model.Evaluate(nn::zeros({16, 64}), memory, beta);
    for (float a : uniform.at("attention").to_vector<float>()) check::Near(a, .1, 1e-7, "zero query uniform attention");
    Save(root / (name + "_zero_control.npz"), uniform);
    std::vector<std::int64_t> reversed;
    for (int c = 0; c < 10; ++c) reversed.push_back(9 - c);
    const auto permutation = model.Evaluate(probes, Rows(memory, reversed), beta);
    const auto probe       = model.Evaluate(probes, memory, beta);
    check::Require(replay::MaxAbsDiff(probe.at("next"), permutation.at("next")) <= 2e-6,
                   "memory permutation preserves retrieval within reduction roundoff");
    Save(root / (name + "_permutation_control.npz"), permutation);
    const auto repeat = model.Evaluate(probes, memory, beta);
    for (const auto& [key, value] : probe) check::Require(Bits(value) == Bits(repeat.at(key)), "fixed input Hopfield repeat bitexact");
    const auto single = model.Evaluate(Rows(probes, {0}), memory, beta);
    check::Require(replay::MaxAbsDiff(single.at("next"), Rows(probe.at("next"), {0})) <= 2e-6, "single batch Hopfield parity");
    const Tensor first_images = WeightedImages(first.at("attention"), memory_gray), final_images = WeightedImages(last.at("attention"), memory_gray);
    const auto   la = last.at("attention").to_vector<float>(), fa = first.at("attention").to_vector<float>();
    const auto   mg = memory_gray.to_vector<float>(), tg = gray[2].to_vector<float>(), ng = noisy_gray, fi = first_images.to_vector<float>(),
               li = final_images.to_vector<float>();
    std::vector<float> gallery(100 * 64), heat(20 * 10);
    for (int row = 0; row < 20; ++row) {
      const auto b      = gallery_indices[row];
      const int  chosen = Argmax(la, b);
      for (int j = 0; j < 64; ++j) {
        gallery[(row * 5) * 64 + j]     = b < 100 ? mg[(b / 10) * 64 + j] : tg[(b - 100) * 64 + j];
        gallery[(row * 5 + 1) * 64 + j] = b < 100 ? ng[b * 64 + j] : tg[(b - 100) * 64 + j];
        gallery[(row * 5 + 2) * 64 + j] = fi[b * 64 + j];
        gallery[(row * 5 + 3) * 64 + j] = li[b * 64 + j];
        gallery[(row * 5 + 4) * 64 + j] = mg[chosen * 64 + j];
      }
      std::copy_n(la.data() + b * 10, 10, heat.data() + row * 10);
    }
    const Tensor gallery_t = nn::from_vector(gallery, {100, 64}), heat_t = nn::from_vector(heat, {20, 10});
    Save(root / (name + "_gallery.npz"),
         {{"images", gallery_t}, {"final_attention", heat_t}, {"first_weighted_images", first_images}, {"final_weighted_images", final_images}});
    Png(root / (name + "_retrieval.png"), gallery_t, 5);
    Heatmap(root / (name + "_attention.png"), heat_t);
    int initial_mem = 0, final_mem = 0, initial_test = 0, final_test = 0;
    for (int b = 0; b < 300; ++b) {
      const int a = Argmax(fa, b), c = Argmax(la, b);
      if (b < 100) initial_mem += a == targets[b], final_mem += c == targets[b];
      else initial_test += a == targets[b], final_test += c == targets[b];
    }
    metrics << beta << '\t' << initial_mem / 100. << '\t' << final_mem / 100. << '\t' << initial_test / 200. << '\t' << final_test / 200.
            << '\t' << energy_increase << '\t' << residual << '\n';
    std::cout << name << ":noisyMemoryAccuracy=" << initial_mem << "->" << final_mem << "/100,heldoutClass=" << initial_test << "->"
              << final_test << "/200,maxEnergyIncrease=" << energy_increase << ",residual=" << residual << std::endl;
  }
  metrics.flush();
  check::Require(memory_bytes == Bits(memory) && query_bytes == Bits(queries_t), "all memory and input bytes immutable");
  std::ofstream meta(root / "metrics.json");
  meta << "{\"trainable_parameters\":0,\"memory_patterns\":10,\"memory_coordinates\":640,\"noisy_memory_queries\":100,\"heldout_"
          "queries\":200,\"retrieval_updates\":8,\"betas\":[1,8,32],\"training_epochs\":0}\n";
  std::ofstream html(root / "index.html");
  html << "<!doctype html><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Modern Hopfield retrieval</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;margin:30px;"
          "max-width:1100px}img{max-width:100%;image-rendering:pixelated}</style><h1>Continuous modern Hopfield associative memory</h1>"
          "<p><a href='https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.02217'>Modern Hopfield</a> energy E(x) = .5||x||^2 - logsumexp(beta M x)/beta. "
          "Retrieval x_next = softmax(beta x M^T) M (tied keys and values, no learned projection or optimizer); the actual energy "
          "gradient equals x - x_next. Real MNIST, half-pixel 28->8 gray, fit-only centering and unit-norm vectors; the first fit "
          "image per class gives 10 stored patterns. 100 noisy-memory queries (+.15 Gaussian) and 200 heldout queries. Datamunge "
          "port of tflow's modern_hopfield.</p><h2>Stored fit memories, classes 0..9</h2><img src='memories.png'>";
  for (int b : {1, 8, 32})
    html << "<h2>beta=" << b << "</h2><p>Columns truth / query / one-update weighted stored image / eight-update weighted stored image "
                                "/ hard-selected stored image; heatmap rows same cases, columns memories 0..9.</p><img src='beta"
         << b << "_retrieval.png'><img src='beta" << b << "_attention.png'>";
  html << "<p>See metrics.tsv and metrics.json.</p>";
  check::Require(bool(metrics) && bool(meta) && bool(html), "complete modern Hopfield records");
  std::cout << "fixedMemory/actualEnergyGrad/energyDescent/zeroQuery/permutation/repeat/singleBatch/immutable PASS\n";

  // ---- TF parity ----
  if (!fs::exists(tf / "metrics.tsv")) {
    std::cout << "no TF record at " << tf.string() << "; parity checks skipped\nArtifacts: " << root.string() << "\n";
    return;
  }
  std::cout << "TF parity (" << tf.string() << "):\n";
  double worst = 0;
  for (const std::string name : {"beta1", "beta8", "beta32"}) {
    worst = std::max(worst, bpix::Compare(tf, name + "_trajectory.npz", Load(root / (name + "_trajectory.npz"))));
    worst = std::max(worst, bpix::Compare(tf, name + "_probe.npz", Load(root / (name + "_probe.npz"))));
    bpix::Compare(tf, name + "_gallery.npz", Load(root / (name + "_gallery.npz")));
  }
  for (int column = 1; column <= 4; ++column) {
    const auto a = replay::History(root / "metrics.tsv", column), b = replay::History(tf / "metrics.tsv", column);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < std::min(a.size(), b.size()); ++i)
      check::Require(std::abs(a[i] - b[i]) < 1e-12, "retrieval accuracies identical to TF's metrics.tsv");
  }
  std::printf("  metrics.tsv accuracies (4 columns x 3 betas) identical to TF's\n");
  check::Require(worst < 1e-4, "trajectories and Jacobian probes match TF's record");
  std::cout << "Artifacts: " << root.string() << "\nAll modern_hopfield checks passed.\n";
}

}  // namespace

int main(int argc, char** argv) {
  try {
    Run(ParseOptions(argc, argv, "modern_hopfield", {{"data", paths::Dataset("saliency").string()}}, "data=PATH out=PATH tf=DIR threads=N"));
    return 0;
  } catch (const std::exception& e) {
    std::cerr << e.what() << '\n';
    return 1;
  }
}

