> Interpretation

Use the computed checks, held-out tables and galleries to assess this bounded run. Exact enumeration is restricted to tiny binary models; CD is a stopped sampled surrogate, and ULA is discretized sampling. The attention and memory fixtures verify mechanisms, not natural-language or long-memory benchmarks. Weak results remain part of the report.

> Held-out retrieval at beta1

The200 test images are classified by the largest final attention weight among the ten fitting-only prototype memories. The100 noisy copies of stored images are excluded from this held-out matrix.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/modern_hopfield_beta1_confusion.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;std::map<std::string,n::Tensor> data,path;for(auto& [k,v]:n::load_npz("build/generative-models/models/modern_hopfield/data.npz"))data[k]=v;for(auto& [k,v]:n::load_npz("build/generative-models/models/modern_hopfield/beta1_trajectory.npz"))path[k]=v;auto truth=n::slice_axis(data.at("target_memory_class"),0,100,300);auto predicted=n::argmax(n::slice_axis(n::select(path.at("attentions"),0,8),0,100,300),1);n::ConfusionMatrix cm(10);cm.add(truth,predicted);cm.save_svg("build/modern_hopfield_beta1_confusion.svg",{.title="Hopfield held-out prototype retrieval: beta1"});n::save_npz("build/modern_hopfield_beta1_confusion.npz",{{"counts",cm.to_tensor()},{"truth",truth},{"predicted",predicted}});std::print("200 held-out queries; truth rows, prediction columns.\n");for(auto& row:cm.cells()){for(auto count:row)std::print("{} ",count);std::print("\n");}}
